This is an LSD radix sort with 11-bit digits, so three scatter passes over 4M values. It uses one temporary buffer of n×4 bytes (about 15 MiB at n = 4M, under the 20 MiB limit). It skips any pass where all values share the same digit, and falls back to heapsort if the allocation fails. I have not compiled or timed it.

