This is an LSD radix sort with three 11-bit passes. It builds all three histograms in one read pass and skips any pass where every element shares the same digit, which helps with the many-duplicates inputs. The scratch buffer is n×4 bytes (16 MiB at n = 4M), within the 20 MiB limit. If `malloc` fails, it falls back to `qsort`. I have not compiled or run it.

