This is an AVX2 bit-parallel scan: each 32-position block ANDs byte-compare masks for each pattern character, and exits early once the mask goes to zero, which happens quickly on a 4-letter alphabet. An SSE2 path (16 lanes) covers builds without AVX2, and a scalar loop handles the tail. Nothing is read past `text[n-1]`, and the only memory is a 2 KiB stack array. I haven't compiled or run it.

