This uses a bitmap over the 2^26 possible values: 8 MiB, under the 10 MiB limit. Each value sets one bit and the count increases when the bit was previously clear. The loop is branchless and prefetches the bitmap word for the element 16 ahead. The bitmap is zeroed with `memset` at the start of each call, so nothing carries over between calls. I have not compiled or timed this.

