This uses Myers/Hyyrö bit-parallel Levenshtein, processing 64 rows per word. For n = m = 6000 that is about 94 blocks × 6000 columns, roughly 0.6M word-steps. The pattern bitmasks are built only for characters that occur in `s`, so memory stays well under the 4 MiB limit. I have not compiled or run it.

