This is an AVX2 implementation that processes 8 pixels per inner loop as two independent 4-lane double vectors. It checks escape before each update, which matches the reference's check-then-iterate order. Early exit happens once every lane has escaped, and the remainder of the iteration budget is handled so no extra iterations are counted. I have not compiled or run it.

