This uses PCLMULQDQ carry-less-multiply folding (the Intel/Chromium-style CRC-32 scheme) for inputs of 64 bytes or more, with a bytewise table for the head/tail remainder. I could not compile or run it, and the fold and Barrett constants are recalled from memory rather than checked against a reference. Only the sub-64-byte path is simple enough to verify by hand, so treat the vector path as untested.

