This is a single-threaded AVX2 kernel that runs four pixels per vector. It keeps an alive mask per lane, so escaped lanes are simply excluded from the count and never need to be frozen. The loop exits early once every lane in a vector has escaped, and it checks for that every eight iterations. A scalar fallback is included in case AVX2 is not enabled at compile time. I have not compiled or run it.

